# SIMAD oLearn: Final Product Walkthrough

This document serves as the final handover for the **SIMAD oLearn Distance Learning Platform** design package. It summarizes the delivered artifacts, technical specifications, and interactive prototypes.

## 1. Executive Summary
We have designed a comprehensive LMS ecosystem branded **SIMAD oLearn**, specifically tailored to handle both routine academic coursework and high-stakes secure examinations ("Exam Shield"). The solution balances accessibility for students with rigorous integrity controls for the institution.

## 2. Deliverables Inventory

### A. Design Specifications
Located in: `internal/design_specs/`

1.  **[PRD & Feature Scope](internal/design_specs/01_PRD_and_Scope.md)**
    *   Defines the "What" and "Why". Includes detailed Functional Requirements (FRs), Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs), and the core feature list for LMS and Assessment engines.
2.  **[Operational Framework](internal/design_specs/02_Roles_and_Processes.md)**
    *   Defines the "Who" and "How". Includes the RACI matrix for 9 user roles and detailed process maps for Course Creation, Exam Lifecycle, and Misconduct handling.
3.  **[Architecture & Roadmap](internal/design_specs/03_Architecture_and_Roadmap.md)**
    *   Defines the "Where" and "When". Outlines the Microservices architecture, Security/Privacy standards (GDPR/Data Retention), and a 3-phase rollout strategy.

